    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Gondwana coal accounts for over 98% of total coal reserves in India, concentrated primarily along the Damodar, Son, Mahanadi, and Godavari river valleys.",
        "Digboi in Assam is India's oldest operational oil field, whereas Mumbai High is the largest offshore petroleum reserve.",
        "The Chota Nagpur Plateau is frequently asked in exams as the 'Ruhr of India' due to its rich repository of mineral wealth."
      ],
